{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A1","title_html":"A1","html":"<p>Consider the following derivation, whose justifications are\nmissing.</p>\n<div class=\"enumerate\" data-options=\"label=(\\alph*)\">\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Write the schema of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{{\\to}I}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2192\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c49\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> from memory, and state\nthe condition that the drawing cannot show.</li>\n<li>Fill in the justifications (i), (ii), (iii), and say what the\nderivation shows, written with <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\vdash\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c22A2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⊢</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</li>\n<li>Which of lines 1–5 are available at line 6, and which boxes?</li>\n<li>Someone extends the derivation by a line 7, the statement <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"R\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D445 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> justified by <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{{\\to}E}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2192\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c45\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> 6, 3. Is the result a\nderivation? If not, name the clause of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"def-derivation\">@def-derivation</span> that line 7\nbreaks.</li>\n<li>In the first derivation in the proof of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"prp-curry\">@prp-curry</span>, why is line 4 available at\nline 5? And why is the inner box closed before the outer one?</li>\n<li>In the same derivation, which rule produces line 5, and which lines\ndoes it cite?</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch1/proving-an-implication.html"}